BEGIN_HYPERDESC
<h1>Damage effects</h1>
What losing parts does to Delta-gliders, each compared with an intact
twin: a landed glider that loses its nose (and nose gear) tips onto it; a
glider in flight that loses its left wing tip rolls to the left; in orbit,
a glider that lost its main engines' part has no main thrust, and one that
lost its left wing tip yaws under main thrust (its centre of gravity moved
off the thrust line) and has smaller moments of inertia.
END_HYPERDESC

